{"name":"Candidate","hex":"#c3bc90","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"candidate","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who seeks to be elected or appointed to a position or privilege.","A person who is thought likely or worthy to gain a position or privilege. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To stand as a candidate for an office, typically for a religious one.","To make or name (something) as a candidate (to be chosen or deemed suitable for a purpose)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/candidate"}],"entries":[{"title":"Candidate","blocks":[{"text":"A candidate, or nominee, is a prospective recipient of an award or honor, or a person seeking or being considered for some kind of position. For example, one can be a candidate for membership in a group or election to an office, in which case a candidate selection occurs."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candidate"},{"title":"Candidate (degree)","blocks":[{"text":"Candidate is the name of various academic degrees, which are today mainly awarded in Scandinavia and Eastern Europe. The degree title was phased out in much of Europe through the 1999 Bologna Process, which has re-formatted academic degrees in Europe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Vitnemaal_candjur.jpg/330px-Vitnemaal_candjur.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candidate_(degree)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Campaign_Signs_DSC02551_%281905616979%29.jpg/500px-Campaign_Signs_DSC02551_%281905616979%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Campaign_Signs_DSC02551_%281905616979%29.jpg/1280px-Campaign_Signs_DSC02551_%281905616979%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbn